## Bashan OS — firmware. Target is an older laptop installed from USB, so
## Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and graphics must work offline, straight off the stick.
## NOTE: firmware-b43-installer and -b43legacy-installer are deliberately
## excluded: they DOWNLOAD firmware at install time, which fails offline.

# Broad base set (free + non-free metapackages)
firmware-linux

# CPU microcode: stability and security fixes on old hardware
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode

# Wi-Fi — the chips actually found in 2008-2020 laptops
firmware-iwlwifi
firmware-realtek
firmware-atheros
firmware-brcm80211
firmware-mediatek
firmware-ti-connectivity
firmware-libertas
firmware-ipw2x00
firmware-ath9k-htc
firmware-carl9170
firmware-zd1211

# Bluetooth lives in these alongside the Wi-Fi blobs
firmware-intel-misc
firmware-misc-nonfree

# Bluetooth firmware for Broadcom BCM203x and CSR adapters, which the two
# packages above do NOT cover. Debian ships this on its own live PC images;
# it was missing from this list until the Part G firmware audit, which is
# exactly the kind of hole hand-curating a list produces.
bluez-firmware

# Graphics
firmware-amd-graphics
firmware-intel-graphics
firmware-nvidia-graphics
# GSP firmware, which nouveau needs on RTX 20-series and newer. Without it
# a modern NVIDIA laptop gets a barely-accelerated desktop out of the box.
# Not the same package as firmware-nvidia-tesla-535-gsp, which is the
# datacenter Tesla branch and stays trimmed.
firmware-nvidia-gsp
firmware-ast

# Audio DSPs: SOF for 2019+ Intel, Cirrus and Realtek codecs
firmware-sof-signed
firmware-intel-sound
firmware-cirrus
